24065	sA surprisingly compact bolt-action anti-materiel rifle, utilizing .50 BMG cartridges. While technically outdated in modern arms markets, it still works exceptionally well in anti-personnel and light anti-armor roles. Also, somehow, capable of fitting a suppressor.
24066	sA surprisingly compact bolt-action anti-materiel rifle, utilizing .50 BMG cartridges. While technically outdated in modern arms markets, it still works exceptionally well in anti-personnel and light anti-armor roles. Also, somehow, capable of fitting a suppressor. This one seems to have a little picture of someone in a Gorlex Marauders blood-red MODsuit stenciled on it, pointing at a green floppy disk. Who knows what that might mean.
24067	sA revival of the ancient SKS semi-automatic rifle, redesigned to utilize .310 Strilka rounds. Loses some per-cartridge stopping power due to quirks in the gas-operation system.
