#rnd_desc
19762	n
19765	sAn experimental surgical procedure that dissects bodies in exchange for research points at ancient R&D consoles.
19778	sA surgical procedure that forces a symbiotic relationship between a virus and its host. The patient will be completely immune to the effects of the virus, but will carry and spread it to others.
19855	sAn experimental procedure which induces the growth of a Romerol tumor inside the patient's brain.
19858	sA surgical procedure which directly implants a directive into the patient's brain, making it their absolute priority. It can be cleared using a mindshield implant.
19859	sInstall malware which directly implants a directive into the robotic patient's operating system, making it their absolute priority. It can be cleared using a mindshield implant.
19862	sAn invasive surgical procedure which guarantees removal of almost all brain traumas, but might cause another permanent trauma in return.
19877	sA surgical procedure which permanently inhibits the aggression center of the brain, making the patient unwilling to cause direct harm.
19878	sInstall malware which permanently inhibits the aggression programming of the patient's neural network, making the patient unwilling to cause direct harm.
19881	sA surgical procedure that repairs damaged wings using Synthflesh.
